<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sayf ibn Dhi Yazan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sayf ibn Dhi Yazan was a semi-legendary Himyarite king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, remembered in Arabic folk tradition. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayfawa-dynasty">Sayfawa dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kanem">Kanem</a> claimed descent from him, and the dynasty took its name from his. The consolidation of power in Kanem is traditionally associated with him, although historically verifiable rulers came later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sayf-ibn-dhi-yazan.jpg" alt="Sayf ibn Dhi Yazan" width="272" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahmed'Aliaan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ali_Bey-_Sultan_Saif-Zuliazan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
